  "notes": "SIMULATION ONLY. A simulated AM-ARM200 (6 joints + gripper) on a table with two blocks and one bin, seen by a simulated overhead camera. Nothing here drives hardware: the simulation robot type refuses a port that is not a sim: name. The arm is the official AM-ARM200 robot description (URDF and meshes from liyiteng/AM-ARM 5b03af1, Apache-2.0, packaged under models/am-arm200): the chain the planner solves is read from it, so link lengths are the published ones. The joint limits and the sign/offset of each joint against the URDF are placeholders not confirmed on a physical arm (verified_on_hardware: false), as is the gripper's jaw-angle mapping. Servo classes follow the lerobot_alohamini am-follower-6dof profile; their ratings are reseller-listed values (see servos.classes.*.source). The scene is laid out inside the arm's reach, off the strip under the arm's ready pose so the overhead camera sees every object.",
